{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams (Bryant,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1986). Each function is a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test variables in index order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a low child for the variable false and a high child for true, down to the constants. No two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices test the same variable with the same children, and none has equal children, so each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function has exactly one root, and checking whether two functions are equal is comparing roots."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import DecisionDiagrams","","var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)       \/\/ 5","diagram.anySatisfyingAssignment(of: f)         \/\/ [false, false, true]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The diagram of ","type":"text"},{"code":"f","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has five vertices: three tests and the two constants. Following the low edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"means the variable is false, the high edge that it is true.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Low child","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"High child"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"root"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"x0","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the test of ","type":"text"},{"code":"x1","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x1"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"true","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"false"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"true"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The test of ","type":"text"},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is shared: ","type":"text"},{"code":"x0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" false and ","type":"text"},{"code":"x0 ∧ ¬x1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" both leave ","type":"text"},{"code":"f","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" equal to ","type":"text"},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so both lead","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the one vertex that stands for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Functions combine under any of the sixteen binary operators with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/apply(_:_:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" in O(|"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"f"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"| |"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"g"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"|), through a computed table of results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already found. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/restrict(_:variable:to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" fixes a variable, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/exists(_:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/forall(_:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" quantify"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over variables. The table’s vertices are a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so Grafluent’s traversals and drawings run over a function’s diagram from its root."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"DecisionDiagrams","externalID":"DecisionDiagrams","modules":[{"name":"DecisionDiagrams"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Binary-decision-diagrams","title":"Binary decision diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Canonical diagrams of Boolean functions."}],"references":{"doc://DecisionDiagrams/documentation/DecisionDiagrams/BinaryDecisionDiagram/GraphView-swift.struct/isHighEdge(at:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/GraphView-swift.struct\/isHighEdge(at:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isHighEdge","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"at","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"isHighEdge(at:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams\/binarydecisiondiagram\/graphview-swift.struct\/ishighedge(at:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the edge is its source’s high edge, taken when the source’s variable is true."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://DecisionDiagrams/documentation/DecisionDiagrams/BinaryDecisionDiagram":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram","url":"\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams\/binarydecisiondiagram","title":"BinaryDecisionDiagram","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A shared table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams: Boolean functions of a fixed number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of variables, each a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test one variable and branch to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"low child (the variable false) and a high child (true), down to the constants (Bryant,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“Graph-Based Algorithms for Boolean Function Manipulation”, 1986)."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram","kind":"id